This is a Rust port of fig2dev 3.2.9a, and parts of it are ported from xfig
and fig2dev (https://mcj.sourceforge.net/). xfig and fig2dev are (c)
1985-1988 Supoj Sutanthavibul, (c) 1991 Micah Beck, and Brian V. Smith, Paul
King, Thomas Loimer and other contributors, under the xfig licence (SPDX:
Xfig), which permits use, modification, sublicensing and redistribution
provided the copyright and permission notice remain intact. That notice is
reproduced in LICENSE-xfig, which also lists every file derived from xfig or
fig2dev with its sources; each of those files names its sources in a comment
and points to LICENSE-xfig.

X-splines are implemented from the published paper: C. Blanc and
C. Schlick, "X-Splines: A Spline Model Designed for the End User",
SIGGRAPH '95.

The AutoCAD slide writer (crates/fig2dev/src/scene/sld.rs) is a port of netpbm's
ppmtoacad (converter/ppm/ppmtoacad.c and autocad.h, including the 256-colour
table), by John Walker, Autodesk SA, 1991: "Permission to use, copy, modify,
and distribute this software and its documentation for any purpose and without
fee is hereby granted, without any conditions or restrictions. This software is
provided "as is" without express or implied warranty."

Assets
------
This repository contains no image, icon or font files. Fill patterns and
colour tables are generated in code.

Fonts used at run time
----------------------
- Installed fonts found at run time with `fontdb` (system fonts, TeX Gyre from
  a TeX installation); none is bundled or redistributed.
- Fallback: Ubuntu Light (Ubuntu Font Licence 1.0) and Hack (MIT/Bitstream
  Vera licence), bundled inside the `epaint_default_fonts` crate (a
  dependency, MIT OR Apache-2.0).

PDF pictures are read with the hayro crates (hayro, hayro-interpret,
hayro-syntax, hayro-write; Laurenz Stampfl, MIT OR Apache-2.0) and their
dependencies (vello_cpu, kurbo, skrifa, moxcms, pic-scale, brotli and
others, all MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-3-Clause, Zlib or similar). The PDF
pictures under crates/fig2dev/tests/pdf_pictures/ and rich.eps there were
written for this repository's tests (MIT OR Apache-2.0).

Third-party Rust crates are used under their own licences (MIT, Apache-2.0,
BSD, Zlib and similar permissive licences); see Cargo.lock.
